  "review": {
    "version": 1,
    "findings": [
      {
        "file": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c",
        "start_line": 672,
        "end_line": 686,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Partially sent multi-segment packet is published without EOP",
        "explanation": "If the loop exits through goto end_of_tx part-way through a packet's segments, the earlier segments have already been copied. last_used has advanced and tx_used entries have been added, but nb_tx_free was not decremented. When nb_tx > 0, used_cnt is published including those segments with no EOP flag. The peer then sees a truncated packet that is never completed. When nb_tx == 0, last_used still advances without being published. This leaves the local and remote ring state inconsistent.",
        "suggestion": "Roll back last_used and nb_mbufs to their values at the start of the packet before jumping to end_of_tx. Alternatively, check that enough descriptors are available for all segments before copying.",
        "evidence": "*txq->used_cnt = txq->last_used;",
        "confidence": 0.5,
        "id": "f459e370fbcc",
        "hunk_id": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c#1",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c",
        "start_line": 755,
        "end_line": 758,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "mbuf alloc failure mid-packet leaves ring state inconsistent and drops data",
        "explanation": "If the refill allocation fails, the code jumps to end_of_rx after last_used has advanced past the current segment. nb_rx is not incremented for that packet, so the caller never receives it and the consumed mbuf leaks. If nb_rx is 0, nothing is published: the descriptors already consumed are never refilled and avail_cnt is not updated. The ring then stalls or loses entries.",
        "suggestion": "Allocate the replacement mbuf before consuming the segment. On failure, restore last_used or stop cleanly without consuming it.",
        "evidence": "NTB_LOG(ERR, \"recv alloc mbuf failed.\");",
        "confidence": 0.45,
        "id": "7c1754b98857",
        "hunk_id": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb.c#2",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
        "tier": 3,
        "escalated_from": [],
        "also_reported_by": []
      },
      {
        "file": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb_hw_intel.c",
        "start_line": 175,
        "end_line": 175,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Off-by-one in ioremap range check",
        "explanation": "The window is [base, base+size), but the check uses <=. An address equal to base+size is accepted and mapped one byte past the BAR. The result is an out-of-bounds write. There is also no check that addr+len stays inside the window.",
        "suggestion": "Use `addr < hw->peer_mw_base[i] + hw->mw_size[i]`.",
        "evidence": "addr <= hw->peer_mw_base[i] + hw->mw_size[i]) {",
        "confidence": 0.6,
        "id": "f619d4257c9d",
        "hunk_id": "drivers/raw/ntb/ntb_hw_intel.c#1",
        "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
